663bbae4-8e84-4909-9aea-6884fefedd89	I feel like landing pages nowadays need to be really, really, really, really, really short. Honestly, like a sentence in length just to describe what the heck you're actually buying and then have a VSL that goes into fairly concise detail of what you're actually buying, right? And then have validation points, you know, all this extra stuff after that. Right? And it doesn't need to be like, honestly, if it could fit, if the landing page can fit on your phone and you don't have to scroll to reach the end of the page, that's a decent sized landing page. Right? And nowadays, in 2025 and going forward, because people are just expecting to get that from ChatGPT. Like, I'm not even lying to you, like, I expect that to get like a response of what exactly is on a website within less than a sentence. Because at the end of the day, like, what new information are you sharing? And like, why can't you describe your whole entire business in less than a sentence? Right? If we can get there and we can get there, like, if we can sell you on that, if we can get you to, like, get the complex and concise and the most detailed, impactful description of your business within a, like, a paragraph slot that is less than the size of your phone screen. Right? Then I feel like you can, you know, really deliver an impactful message, plus a video sales letter.	{"Landing Page Efficiency","Future of Web Design","User Experience Expectations","Impact of AI on Web Content"}	{"really, really, really, really, really short","if the landing page can fit on your phone","expecting to get that from ChatGPT","describe your whole entire business in less than a sentence"}	energetic	fast	{"0:15": "Introduction of the concept of ultra-short landing pages", "0:30": "Mention of ChatGPT setting new expectations", "0:45": "Challenge to describe a business in less than a sentence"}	75	3.0	2025-12-25 00:47:56.573001+00	{"mood": "casual", "colors": ["light blue", "green", "grey"], "