748470b3-0507-49d5-9ad1-94a0e8f11674	Tell me what, ask me what I'm doing. What are you doing? So I'm thinking about putting, right now I'm hearing from, so from looking at this fan, I am noticing that I hear a pressure differential from this ear to that ear because by the wind moving across the surface of my face being generated. And this, you know, from that fan, it's causing the wind to shirk off my face and cause a higher pressure differential from this ear to that ear. And it's making me sense a high pitch noise that I know is not coming from anything else except for the air disturbance. So I'm thinking about probably applying some type of blunt modifications to the blade tips to the blade tips of this single stage compressor to make that pressure differential go away when specifically laying in this position on this bed and this in this manner. And I'm pretty sure if I turned around, I would not hear that same pressure differential. But, you know, since this is where I like to sit and lay, I think I might do that. I think.	{"Physics of everyday objects","DIY solutions to common problems","Personal anecdotes related to science","The impact of environment on human senses"}	{"Tell me what, ask me what I'm doing.","I am noticing that I hear a pressure differential from this ear to that ear.","I'm thinking about probably applying some type of blunt modifications to the blade tips."}	educational	medium	{"00:00": "Introduction to the problem", "00:30": "Explanation of the pressure differential", "01:00": "Proposed solution to modify fan blades"}	65	3.0	2025-12-25 06:48:57.86569+00	{"mood": "serene and relaxed", "colors": ["light gray", "white", "brown"], "frame_count": 5, "deep_analysis": {"title": "Cozy Morning in Bed", "people": [{"position": "center right", "body_pose": "Lying down, head slightly tilted to the side", "person_id": 1, "accessories": [], "clothing_style": "casual", "ethnicity_note": null, "gaze_direction": "towards the camera", "apparent_action": "res